{%- comment -%}
  Renders a hex color for a given rarity tag value. Confirmed live across
  all 8 games with an internal catalog (see docs/catalog-audit.md) by
  reading each game's filter-sidebar rarity checkbox SVG fill color — the
  same colors bloxcart.com itself uses for its accent bars. No two games
  contradict each other on a shared rarity name (e.g. "common" is
  #DCDCF9 everywhere it appears), so one flat lookup covers all of them;
  MM2's Godly/Ancient/Unique are the only genuinely game-specific tiers.

  Note: on the source site, several rarity NAMES share the same color
  within a game (Steal a Brainrot's "secret" and "og" are both #C0C0C0;
  Blox Fruits' "uncommon"/"common" likewise) — that makes color -> name
  lookups ambiguous, not this direction (name -> color), so it's safe here.
  data/catalog.json only sets rarity_name where it was unambiguous;
  ambiguous products simply don't pass a `rarity` param in here at all.

  TODO (Phase 8 data import): move this to a `custom.rarity_color`
  metafield per product so merchandisers can adjust without a code
  deploy — this snippet is a stopgap until that metafield exists.

  Usage: {% render 'rarity-color', rarity: 'godly' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = rarity | downcase
  case key
    when 'godly'
      echo '#FF643A'
    when 'ancient'
      echo '#C84CFF'
    when 'unique'
      echo '#FF4F59'
    when 'common'
      echo '#DCDCF9'
    when 'uncommon'
      echo '#DCDCF9'
    when 'rare'
      echo '#4891FF'
    when 'legendary'
      echo '#68D74D'
    when 'ultra-rare'
      echo '#FF4FD8'
    when 'secret'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    when 'og'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    when 'mythical'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    when 'mythic'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    when 'super'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    when 'exclusive'
      echo '#C0C0C0'
    else
      echo settings.color_accent
  endcase
-%}
